---
/**
 * Brief behind the "Oil keeps prices and rates high" row on /risk/. Backstory
 * is dated text. Where we stand and the levels in What we're watching are
 * built from the row's feeds at build time (src/lib/briefs.ts), so they move
 * with every feed push. No oil number is written by hand on this page. The
 * long essay that lived here is in docs/archive/pages/economics/.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { oilBriefNow } from '../../lib/briefs';
import '../../styles/economics.css';

const title = 'Oil keeps prices and rates high';
const subhead = 'Oil was above $100 at the Fed\'s first rate hike. Higher oil pushes prices up and keeps rates high. The numbers below come from the /risk/ watch-list feed.';

const brief = oilBriefNow();

const watchItems = [
  ...brief.watch,
  '27 to 28 Oct 2026: the next FOMC meeting.',
  "PCE inflation reports, set against the Fed's 3.7% median forecast for 2026.",
];

const sources = [
  { text: 'Federal Reserve, FOMC statement, 16 Sep 2026', href: 'https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20260916a.htm' },
  { text: 'Federal Reserve, Summary of Economic Projections, 16 Sep 2026', href: 'https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomcprojtabl20260916.htm' },
  { text: 'Reuters, oil prices on 16 Sep 2026', href: 'https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/oil-falls-us-crude-inventories-rise-despite-saudi-supply-concerns-2026-09-16/' },
  { text: 'Yahoo Finance, WTI crude futures (CL=F) price history', href: 'https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CL=F/history/' },
  { text: 'U.S. Treasury, Daily Treasury Par Yield Curve Rates', href: 'https://home.treasury.gov/resource-center/data-chart-center/interest-rates/TextView?type=daily_treasury_yield_curve&field_tdr_date_value=2026' },
  { text: 'Federal Reserve, FOMC meeting calendar', href: 'https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm' },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} - Rycode`}
  description={subhead}
  variant="economics"
>
  <article class="econ-digest econ-digest--body econ-brief">
    <header class="econ-digest-head">
      <h1 class="econ-digest-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="econ-digest-subhead">{subhead}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="backstory">
      <h2>Backstory</h2>
      <p>On 16 Sep 2026 the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC), the Fed body that sets short-term interest rates, raised its target for the federal funds rate, the overnight rate banks charge each other, by a quarter point to 3.75% to 4.00%. The vote was 12 to 0. It was Kevin Warsh's first rate increase as Fed Chair. The statement said inflation remains elevated and gave no schedule for future moves.</p>
      <p>The Fed's projections put the median year-end funds rate at 4.1%, above the new range's midpoint of 3.875%. The median forecast for 2026 PCE inflation, the Fed's preferred price gauge, rose to 3.7% from 3.6% in June. A high 10-year Treasury yield, the rate the government pays to borrow for ten years, makes future company profits worth less today, which weighs on stock prices.</p>
      <p>Oil was the other pressure. Brent and West Texas Intermediate (WTI), the main world and US crude benchmarks, both settled above $100 a barrel on the day of the hike even after falling, according to Reuters. Oil that high keeps energy feeding inflation, which works against the Fed's goal of getting inflation back to 2%.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="where-we-stand">
      <h2>Where we stand</h2>
      <p class="econ-brief-asof">{brief.asOf}</p>
      <p>{brief.level}</p>
      <p>{brief.range}</p>
      <p>{brief.rates}</p>
      <p>{brief.strain}</p>
    </section>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="watching">
      <h2>What we're watching</h2>
      <ul class="econ-brief-watch">
        {watchItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="econ-digest-section econ-digest-sources" id="sources">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ol>
        {sources.map((source) => (
          <li>
            <a href={source.href}>{source.text}</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .econ-brief .econ-digest-section {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .econ-brief .econ-digest-section > p.econ-brief-asof {
    margin: -0.35rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--digest-faint, rgba(248, 250, 252, 0.4));
  }

  .econ-brief-watch {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 1.35rem;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 40rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .econ-brief-watch li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--digest-ink);
  }

  .econ-brief-watch li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 0.38rem;
    height: 0.38rem;
    background: currentColor;
  }
</style>
